# Rust
target/
*.rlib
*.rmeta
# Cargo.lock is intentionally checked in (both the workspace root
# and `python/Cargo.lock`) — this workspace ships a binary
# (`aresadb-cluster`), a Docker image, and a PyO3 wheel
# (`aresadb-python`) that all need reproducible builds. Downstream
# library consumers still get semver-compatible resolution via
# `cargo update` on their side.

